SIM-25: apply a pump power set while the solver is open

EN_setlinkvalue(EN_PUMP_POWER) stores the power and marks the pump as
constant power, but the pump's head curve coefficients are derived only
by validateproject() at EN_openH. During a run a constant-power pump
kept its old power, and a curve pump switched to constant power used
its old curve coefficients in the constant-power formula and delivered
no head. Call updatepumpparams() (added by SIM-22) when the solver is
open, as SIM-22 does for EN_setheadcurveindex and EN_setcurve.

Requires: SIM-03 SIM-22

Apply from the root of an EPANET checkout at 83e25bb, after SIM-03,
SIM-22 and the patches SIM-22 requires:
    git apply SIM-03_fix.patch
    git apply CRASH-16_fix.patch
    git apply SIM-19_fix.patch
    git apply SIM-21_fix.patch
    git apply SIM-17_fix.patch
    git apply SIM-22_fix.patch
    git apply SIM-25_fix.patch

diff --git a/src/epanet.c b/src/epanet.c
index 5ce8c95..b0890e0 100644
--- a/src/epanet.c
+++ b/src/epanet.c
@@ -4303,6 +4303,10 @@ int DLLEXPORT EN_setlinkvalue(EN_Project p, int index, int property, double valu
             net->Pump[pumpIndex].Ptype = CONST_HP;
             net->Pump[pumpIndex].Hcurve = 0;
             net->Link[index].Km = value / Ucf[POWER];
+
+            // If the hydraulic solver is open, update the pump's
+            // coefficients now (otherwise EN_openH does this)
+            if (hyd->OpenHflag) updatepumpparams(p, pumpIndex);
         }
         break;
 
